# Welcome to **Tasking**

## Your Personal Task Management System

**Zip Code Wilmington**

---

# What is Tasking?

A **multi-tenant web application** designed specifically for students and instructors

✅ **Personal Task Management** - Create and track your own tasks
✅ **Instructor Assignments** - Receive tasks from instructors  
✅ **Visual Organization** - Kanban board workflow
✅ **Progress Tracking** - Monitor completion status
✅ **Cohort Integration** - Organized by your cohort

---

# Why Use Tasking?

During your bootcamp, you'll juggle:

- 📝 Individual programming labs
- 👥 Group programming projects  
- 📚 Reading assignments
- 📄 Documentation tasks
- 💼 Resume building
- 🚀 Professional development
- 🎤 Demo presentations

**Tasking helps you see everything in one place**

---

# Understanding Kanban

**Kanban** (看板) = "visual signal" in Japanese

Originally from manufacturing, now widely used in software development

### Why it works:
- **Visualize** all your work at once
- **Limit** work in progress
- **Improve** workflow
- **Identify** bottlenecks
- **Track** progress

---

# The Four Columns

### 📋 **Pending** (To Do)
Tasks you haven't started yet - your backlog

### 🔄 **In Progress** (Doing)  
Tasks you're actively working on - limit these!

### 🚧 **Blocked** (Stuck)
Tasks stopped by dependencies - need help

### ✅ **Completed** (Done)
Finished tasks - celebrate your progress!

---

# Your Dashboard

![w:900](https://via.placeholder.com/900x400/2563eb/ffffff?text=Kanban+Board+View)

- **Header** - Username, role, logout
- **Action Buttons** - Add tasks, view groups
- **Kanban Board** - Four columns with task cards
- **Drag & Drop** - Move tasks between columns

---

# Task Categories (Part 1)

**9 task types** to organize your work:

- 👥 **Group Programming Project** - Team coding assignments
- 💻 **Individual Programming Lab** - Solo coding exercises
- 📚 **Reading** - Textbooks, docs, articles
- 📄 **Documentation** - README files, technical writing
- 📝 **Resume** - Building your professional resume

---

# Task Categories (Part 2)

More task types:

- 🚀 **ProDev** - Professional development, networking
- 🎤 **Demo/Presentation** - Project demos, presentations
- 🔬 **Research/Analysis/Design** - System design, architecture
- 📊 **Organize** - Planning and meta-work

**Each type has a color-coded badge for quick visual identification**

---

# Daily Workflow

### Morning (5 min)
✓ Check Pending - what's due?
✓ Review In Progress - what can you finish?
✓ Check for new instructor tasks

### During the Day
✓ Move tasks as you work on them
✓ Mark Blocked if stuck
✓ Move to Completed when done

### Evening (5 min)
✓ Update statuses
✓ Plan for tomorrow

---

# Managing Work in Progress

### 🎯 **Limit your WIP**
Keep only **2-3 tasks** "In Progress" at once

### Why?
- Multiple partial tasks = nothing done
- Context switching is expensive
- Focus = better quality work
- **Finished is better than perfect**

### Rule of thumb:
**Stop starting, start finishing!**

---

# Instructor-Assigned Tasks

### Types of assignments:
1. **Individual** - Assigned directly to you
2. **Cohort** - Assigned to entire cohort
3. **Group** - Assigned to specific team

### What you can do:
✅ View details and requirements
✅ Update status (move between columns)
✅ Mark as Blocked if you need help

### What you cannot do:
❌ Delete or edit instructor tasks

---

# What Instructors Can See

### ✅ Instructors CAN:
- View your Kanban board
- See task statuses and progress
- Identify students who need help
- Track cohort-wide completion

### ❌ Instructors CANNOT:
- Move your tasks between columns
- Edit your personal tasks
- Delete your tasks
- Change your statuses

**You own your board and your progress!**

---

# Tasking vs Other Tools

### **GitHub Projects**
Best for: Repository-specific work, issues, PRs
Use for: Managing code within a single project

### **Trello**  
Best for: General-purpose project management
Use for: Personal life, side projects

### **Tasking**
Best for: **All your bootcamp work in one place**
Use for: Course assignments, readings, professional development

**Many students use all three together!**

---

# Best Practices

### ✅ **Do This:**
- Start each day with your board
- Keep tasks small (hours, not days)
- Update at least twice daily
- Use the Blocked status when stuck
- Add resource URLs for quick access

### ❌ **Avoid This:**
- Having 10+ tasks In Progress
- Ignoring instructor assignments
- Keeping everything in Pending
- Working in silence when blocked

---

# Getting Started

### Three Simple Steps:

1. **Log in** with your credentials
2. **Review** any instructor-assigned tasks
3. **Create** your first personal task

